      "end_seconds": 5.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.37,
      "end_seconds": 9.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "good morning, doctor, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.34,
      "end_seconds": 12.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Where shall we begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.5,
      "end_seconds": 20.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "I, I wanted to get a painful ulcer that is growing quickly looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.21,
      "end_seconds": 29.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Okay, when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.49,
      "end_seconds": 38.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "it's been two months, I'm fairly sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.95,
      "end_seconds": 42.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.96,
      "end_seconds": 47.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "I'd say a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.14,
      "end_seconds": 52.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "So, how much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.23,
      "end_seconds": 55.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "It feels severe to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.08,
      "end_seconds": 60.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.45,
      "end_seconds": 67.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Severe pain goes along with it, most of the time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.11,
      "end_seconds": 72.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.65,
      "end_seconds": 76.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "No, nothing at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.62,
      "end_seconds": 81.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "any regular medication, tablets or creams?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.26,
      "end_seconds": 84.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Nothing regular, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.38,
      "end_seconds": 100.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.61,
      "end_seconds": 104.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.91,
      "end_seconds": 109.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.64,
      "end_seconds": 115.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.8,
      "end_seconds": 120.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.52,
      "end_seconds": 124.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.24,
      "end_seconds": 126.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.06,
      "end_seconds": 132.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.86,
      "end_seconds": 141.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.97,
      "end_seconds": 145.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.87,
      "end_seconds": 167.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "did you get recent cut, fever, diabetes or recent injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.84,
      "end_seconds": 170.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.64,
      "end_seconds": 174.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.27,
      "end_seconds": 178.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.15,
      "end_seconds": 192.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.24,
      "end_seconds": 203.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.49,
      "end_seconds": 228.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 117 over 68, heart rate 80, temperature 36.7. And oxygen saturation is 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.62,
      "end_seconds": 234.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.11,
      "end_seconds": 237.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.1,
      "end_seconds": 261.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "The ulcer has a ragged purple edge with a boggy base and and undermined borders."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.51,
      "end_seconds": 265.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.26,
      "end_seconds": 294.32,
      "duration_seconds": 17.06,
      "text": "taking everything into account, I'd lean towards possible pyoderma gangrenosum linked to bowel inflammation i'd like to arrange a stool test for bowel symptoms that will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.44,
      "end_seconds": 296.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.19,
      "end_seconds": 327.16,
      "duration_seconds": 29.97,
      "text": "We should do a skin biopsy for rapidly enlarging ulcer. Do not cut or scrub it, that can make it worse. The dermatology clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you. Let's hold off on blood tests for now, and if there's no change next month we can revisit it. I'd like to see you again after the biopsy. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.92,
      "end_seconds": 334.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "oh, um, I think I understand everything. Thanks"
    }
  ]
